1
00:00:01,335 --> 00:00:03,295
( rooster crows )

2
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:06,340
( crowing )

3
00:00:08,007 --> 00:00:10,845
( crowing )

4
00:00:10,886 --> 00:00:13,764
WHAT THE HELL
IS THAT?

5
00:00:13,806 --> 00:00:16,433
( crowing )

6
00:00:16,475 --> 00:00:18,435
WHAT THE HELL IS THAT?

7
00:00:18,477 --> 00:00:20,437
IS THAT YOU?

8
00:00:20,479 --> 00:00:22,940
( crowing )

9
00:00:22,982 --> 00:00:25,651
OH!

10
00:00:25,693 --> 00:00:28,612
BOY, YOU ARE REALLY
NOT A MORNING PERSON.

11
00:00:28,654 --> 00:00:30,155
BACK OFF!

12
00:00:31,907 --> 00:00:34,910
GET UP! GET UP! GET UP!

13
00:00:34,952 --> 00:00:35,911
GET UP! GET UP!

14
00:00:35,953 --> 00:00:38,205
GET UP! GET UP! GET UP!

15
00:00:40,123 --> 00:00:42,751
WHAT IS THAT NOISE?

16
00:00:42,793 --> 00:00:44,294
YOU.

17
00:00:46,005 --> 00:00:47,589
IT'S THE CHICK.

18
00:00:47,631 --> 00:00:51,218
SHE'S GOING
THROUGH SOME CHANGES.

19
00:00:51,259 --> 00:00:53,804
WHAT KIND
OF CHANGES?

20
00:00:53,846 --> 00:00:55,430
THE VET SEEMS TO THINK

21
00:00:55,472 --> 00:00:57,725
THAT SHE'S BECOMING
A ROOSTER.

22
00:00:57,766 --> 00:01:00,769
( crowing )

23
00:01:00,811 --> 00:01:03,230
WE'RE GETTING
A SECOND OPINION.

24
00:01:09,945 --> 00:01:13,908
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

25
00:01:13,949 --> 00:01:17,202
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

26
00:01:17,244 --> 00:01:19,580
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

27
00:01:19,621 --> 00:01:23,458
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

28
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:26,085
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

29
00:01:26,127 --> 00:01:29,757
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

30
00:01:29,798 --> 00:01:33,594
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

31
00:01:33,635 --> 00:01:35,930
♪ WHEN THE RAIN STARTS TO POUR ♪

32
00:01:35,971 --> 00:01:38,640
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

33
00:01:38,682 --> 00:01:41,268
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

34
00:01:41,309 --> 00:01:43,186
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

35
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:45,397
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

36
00:01:53,781 --> 00:01:54,907
HEY.

37
00:01:54,949 --> 00:01:56,450
WHAT ARE YOU
DOING SHOPPING

38
00:01:56,491 --> 00:01:57,785
AT 8:00 IN
THE MORNING?

39
00:01:57,826 --> 00:01:59,453
WELL, I'VE BEEN UP
SINCE 6:00

40
00:01:59,494 --> 00:02:01,705
THANKS TO SOMEBODY'S
DUMB-ASS ROOSTER.

41
00:02:01,747 --> 00:02:03,498
GUYS, YOU REALLY
SHOULD GET RID

42
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:04,750
OF THOSE ANIMALS.

43
00:02:04,792 --> 00:02:06,794
THEY SHOULDN'T BE LIVING
IN AN APARTMENT.

44
00:02:06,835 --> 00:02:10,297
ESPECIALLY NOT WITH ALL THESE
KNIVES AND COOKBOOKS AROUND.

45
00:02:12,257 --> 00:02:15,385
ALL RIGHT, I'M GOING TO GO
TO THE FERTILITY DOCTOR

46
00:02:15,427 --> 00:02:18,305
AND SEE IF I'M READY TO HAVE
FRANK AND ALICE'S EMBRYO

47
00:02:18,346 --> 00:02:19,890
TRANSFERRED INTO MY UTERUS.

48
00:02:19,932 --> 00:02:22,893
NOW, HOW WILL THEY KNOW
IF YOU'RE READY?

49
00:02:22,935 --> 00:02:24,227
THEY'RE GOING TO SEE

50
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:26,396
IF MY ENDOMETRIAL LAYER
IS THICK.

51
00:02:26,438 --> 00:02:29,399
WELL, I CAN, UH, CHECK THAT
FOR YOU.

52
00:02:29,441 --> 00:02:31,359
OKAY, EVERYONE, THINK THICK.

53
00:02:31,401 --> 00:02:33,403
GOOD LUCK.
GOOD LUCK.

54
00:02:33,445 --> 00:02:34,613
HEY!
HEY!

55
00:02:34,655 --> 00:02:35,948
WISH ME LUCK.

56
00:02:35,990 --> 00:02:37,449
OH... GOOD LUCK.

57
00:02:37,491 --> 00:02:38,951
AND I'M STILL RIGHT.

58
00:02:38,993 --> 00:02:40,953
THAT IS SO NOT TRUE.

59
00:02:40,995 --> 00:02:42,370
WHAT?

60
00:02:42,412 --> 00:02:44,915
SHE'S MAD BECAUSE I KNOW
TODAY'S HER LAUNDRY DAY

61
00:02:44,957 --> 00:02:48,127
AND THAT MEANS SHE'S WEARING
HER OLD LADY UNDERPANTS.

62
00:02:50,004 --> 00:02:53,298
WELL, I CAN
CHECK THAT FOR YOU.

63
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:55,216
I JUST CAN'T BELIEVE
THAT YOU THINK

64
00:02:55,258 --> 00:02:56,677
THAT YOU AND CHANDLER
KNOW ME AND RACHEL BETTER

65
00:02:56,718 --> 00:02:58,345
THAN WE KNOW YOU.

66
00:02:58,386 --> 00:03:00,681
WELL, WE DO.

67
00:03:00,722 --> 00:03:03,851
YOU CAN ONLY EAT TIC TACS
IN EVEN NUMBERS.

68
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:05,769
YEAH, WHAT'S THAT ABOUT?

69
00:03:05,811 --> 00:03:07,729
AND YOU...

70
00:03:07,771 --> 00:03:10,189
ROSS, I BELIEVE IF
YOU CHECK RACHEL'S BAG

71
00:03:10,231 --> 00:03:13,234
YOU WILL FIND A HALF-EATEN BOX
OF COOKIES IN THERE.

72
00:03:17,072 --> 00:03:18,740
YOU'RE GOOD.

73
00:03:20,159 --> 00:03:22,201
THESE ARE NOT.

74
00:03:22,243 --> 00:03:23,620
SO NOT IMPRESSED.

75
00:03:23,662 --> 00:03:25,747
EVERYBODY SNACKS
WHEN THEY SHOP.

76
00:03:25,789 --> 00:03:26,957
OH, YEAH?

77
00:03:26,999 --> 00:03:29,292
ROSS, HOW MANY ITEMS
LEFT IN THAT BAG?

78
00:03:29,334 --> 00:03:30,418
FIVE.

79
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:32,253
OKAY, TEN BUCKS SAYS

80
00:03:32,295 --> 00:03:35,966
THAT WE CAN NAME
EVERY ITEM IN THAT BAG.

81
00:03:36,008 --> 00:03:37,592
HOW MANY GUESSES DO YOU GET?

82
00:03:37,634 --> 00:03:38,760
SIX.

83
00:03:38,802 --> 00:03:40,554
CHALLENGE EXTENDED.

84
00:03:40,595 --> 00:03:42,764
DEAL.

85
00:03:42,806 --> 00:03:45,350
CHALLENGE ACCEPTED.

86
00:03:45,392 --> 00:03:47,352
ALL RIGHT.

87
00:03:47,394 --> 00:03:48,854
WE'LL START WITH...

88
00:03:48,896 --> 00:03:50,731
APPLES.

89
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:53,984
WE'LL BE STARTING WITH APPLES.

90
00:03:55,986 --> 00:03:57,696
STOP THAT NOW.

91
00:03:59,238 --> 00:04:00,323
YES.

92
00:04:00,365 --> 00:04:03,451
OKAY, UH, TORTILLA
CHIPS, YOGURT...

93
00:04:03,493 --> 00:04:05,162
DIET SODA...

94
00:04:05,204 --> 00:04:06,663
YES, YES...

95
00:04:06,705 --> 00:04:07,956
YES.

96
00:04:09,666 --> 00:04:10,751
ORANGE JUICE.

97
00:04:10,792 --> 00:04:12,251
THERE'S NO ORANGE JUICE
IN THERE.

98
00:04:12,293 --> 00:04:13,253
WE WIN!

99
00:04:13,294 --> 00:04:15,547
THEY HAVE ANOTHER GUESS.

100
00:04:15,589 --> 00:04:19,342
OKAY, WELL, WE WON THAT ONE.

101
00:04:19,384 --> 00:04:21,678
OKAY, THE LAST THING IS...

102
00:04:21,720 --> 00:04:23,722
OOH, OOH! OOH! OOH, OOH!

103
00:04:25,724 --> 00:04:28,518
NO. NO. NOT FOR LIKE
ANOTHER TWO WEEKS.

104
00:04:31,312 --> 00:04:32,773
I GOT IT.

105
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:34,191
SCOTCH...

106
00:04:34,233 --> 00:04:35,358
TAPE.

107
00:04:37,236 --> 00:04:38,403
HA!

108
00:04:40,614 --> 00:04:43,491
HOW DID YOU KNOW
SHE WOULD BUY SCOTCH TAPE?

109
00:04:43,533 --> 00:04:46,703
WELL, WE USED UP THEIRS
LAST NIGHT MAKING SCARY FACES.

110
00:04:48,205 --> 00:04:49,539
OH, MAN.

111
00:04:49,581 --> 00:04:51,166
ALL RIGHT, TEN BUCKS.

112
00:04:51,208 --> 00:04:52,333
FORK IT OVER.

113
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:53,668
COUGH IT UP.

114
00:04:53,710 --> 00:04:55,963
PAY THE PIPER.

115
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:58,006
GIVE ME IT.

116
00:04:58,048 --> 00:05:00,175
THAT DOES NOT MEAN
YOU KNOW US BETTER.

117
00:05:00,217 --> 00:05:01,509
I WANT A REMATCH.

118
00:05:01,551 --> 00:05:03,720
AND NONE OF THESE
STUPID GROCERY QUESTIONS.

119
00:05:03,762 --> 00:05:05,097
REAL PERSONAL QUESTIONS.

120
00:05:05,139 --> 00:05:07,557
YEAH, AND THE WINNER
GETS A HUNDRED BUCKS.

121
00:05:07,599 --> 00:05:09,143
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

122
00:05:09,184 --> 00:05:11,686
ARE YOU SCARED?

123
00:05:13,188 --> 00:05:14,564
( fearfully ):
NO.

124
00:05:14,606 --> 00:05:18,443
OKAY, WHO MAKES UP
THE QUESTIONS?

125
00:05:18,485 --> 00:05:20,195
ROSS'LL DO IT.

126
00:05:20,237 --> 00:05:21,947
OH, SURE,
ROSS'LL DO IT.

127
00:05:21,989 --> 00:05:24,741
IT'S NOT LIKE HE HAS
A JOB OR A CHILD

128
00:05:24,783 --> 00:05:26,367
OR A LIFE OF HIS OWN.

129
00:05:26,409 --> 00:05:28,411
WELL, FINE.
WE'LL ASK PHOEBE.

130
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:29,871
NO. I WANT TO PLAY.

131
00:05:34,126 --> 00:05:35,794
LOOKS LIKE
YOUR UTERUS

132
00:05:35,836 --> 00:05:37,921
IS READY FOR
IMPLANTATION.

133
00:05:37,963 --> 00:05:39,464
OH, I KNEW IT.

134
00:05:39,506 --> 00:05:41,842
I FELT REALLY THICK
THIS MORNING.

135
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:43,760
WELL, OKAY,
SO, WHAT'S NOW?

136
00:05:43,802 --> 00:05:45,179
GO-GO GET THE EGGS.

137
00:05:45,220 --> 00:05:46,554
PUT THEM IN THERE.

138
00:05:46,596 --> 00:05:48,765
OKAY. IT'LL TAKE
JUST A LITTLE WHILE

139
00:05:48,807 --> 00:05:50,225
TO PREPARE THE EMBRYOS.

140
00:05:50,267 --> 00:05:51,226
EMBRYOS?

141
00:05:51,268 --> 00:05:52,727
AS IN MORE THAN ONE.

142
00:05:52,769 --> 00:05:54,271
FIVE, ACTUALLY.

143
00:05:54,313 --> 00:05:56,273
FIVE? OKAY,
WHERE AM I GIVING BIRTH?

144
00:05:56,315 --> 00:05:58,900
IN A HOSPITAL
OR A BIG BOX UNDER THE STAIRS?

145
00:05:58,942 --> 00:06:00,235
WE DO FIVE

146
00:06:00,277 --> 00:06:02,737
BECAUSE THAT GIVES YOU
A 25% CHANCE

147
00:06:02,779 --> 00:06:04,531
THAT AT LEAST
ONE WILL ATTACH.

148
00:06:04,572 --> 00:06:06,116
THAT'S IT? 25 PERCENT?

149
00:06:06,158 --> 00:06:07,575
THAT MEANS THAT IT'S

150
00:06:07,617 --> 00:06:10,578
LIKE 75 PERCENT CHANCE
OF NO BABY AT ALL?

151
00:06:10,620 --> 00:06:12,455
YEAH, YOU KNOW,
I WAS THINKING.

152
00:06:12,497 --> 00:06:15,750
WHAT ARE THE ODDS
IF YOU STUFF 200
OF THEM IN THERE?

153
00:06:17,211 --> 00:06:19,378
SWEETIE,
NOW, SHE'S A WOMAN

154
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:21,298
NOT A GUM BALL MACHINE.

155
00:06:23,466 --> 00:06:25,302
OKAY, WELL, DON'T
WORRY, YOU GUYS

156
00:06:25,344 --> 00:06:28,180
'CAUSE I'M GOING TO DO THIS
AS MANY TIMES AS IT TAKES

157
00:06:28,222 --> 00:06:29,348
TO GET IT RIGHT.

158
00:06:29,388 --> 00:06:31,390
WELL, SEE, THE THING IS

159
00:06:31,432 --> 00:06:33,977
WE KIND OF ONLY HAVE
ONE SHOT.

160
00:06:34,019 --> 00:06:37,314
IT COSTS $16,000
EACH TIME YOU DO THIS.

161
00:06:37,356 --> 00:06:39,398
SO, UM...

162
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:41,609
WE'RE KIND OF USING
ALL THE MONEY WE HAVE

163
00:06:41,651 --> 00:06:43,111
TO DO IT
JUST THIS ONE TIME.

164
00:06:43,153 --> 00:06:44,946
WHOA!

165
00:06:44,988 --> 00:06:47,532
THAT'S... OKAY, THAT'S
A LOT OF PRESSURE

166
00:06:47,574 --> 00:06:49,159
ON ME AND MY UTERUS.

167
00:06:49,201 --> 00:06:52,329
SO, WELL, OKAY...
SO, MAYBE THERE'S
SOMETHING I CAN DO

168
00:06:52,371 --> 00:06:53,705
YOU KNOW

169
00:06:53,747 --> 00:06:56,124
JUST TO, LIKE, HELP
MAKE SURE I GET PREGNANT.

170
00:06:56,166 --> 00:06:57,667
NO. I'M SORRY.

171
00:06:57,709 --> 00:07:00,587
WOW. YOU GUYS
REALLY DON'T KNOW ANYTHING.

172
00:07:01,796 --> 00:07:03,506
WHY DON'T YOU GET DRUNK?

173
00:07:03,548 --> 00:07:04,423
THAT WORKED
FOR A BUNCH OF GIRLS

174
00:07:04,465 --> 00:07:05,967
IN MY HIGH SCHOOL.

175
00:07:11,265 --> 00:07:13,016
HEY, GUYS,
DO YOU REALIZE

176
00:07:13,058 --> 00:07:16,395
THAT ANY MINUTE NOW,
PHOEBE COULD BE PREGNANT.

177
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:17,729
I KNOW. I KNOW.

178
00:07:17,771 --> 00:07:20,857
IT'S SUCH A HUGE,
LIFE-ALTERING THING.

179
00:07:20,899 --> 00:07:23,651
I KNOW.
IT IS.

180
00:07:23,693 --> 00:07:24,485
THE TEST IS READY.

181
00:07:24,527 --> 00:07:27,530
( cheering )

182
00:07:27,572 --> 00:07:31,659
OKAY, EACH TEAM WILL
ANSWER TEN QUESTIONS.

183
00:07:31,701 --> 00:07:36,497
THE FIRST TEAM TO ANSWER
THE MOST QUESTIONS WINS.

184
00:07:36,539 --> 00:07:39,709
THE CATEGORIES ARE
"FEARS AND PET PEEVES"

185
00:07:39,751 --> 00:07:41,753
"ANCIENT HISTORY"

186
00:07:41,795 --> 00:07:43,588
"LITERATURE"

187
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:46,425
AND "IT'S ALL RELATIVE."

188
00:07:46,465 --> 00:07:48,927
NOW...

189
00:07:48,969 --> 00:07:53,307
THE COIN TOSS,
TO SEE WHO GOES FIRST.

190
00:07:59,813 --> 00:08:01,064
OKAY...

191
00:08:01,106 --> 00:08:03,233
SOMEBODY CALL IT THIS TIME.

192
00:08:03,275 --> 00:08:04,901
YEAH. OKAY.

193
00:08:04,943 --> 00:08:06,861
TAILS!

194
00:08:06,903 --> 00:08:07,988
IT'S HEADS.

195
00:08:08,029 --> 00:08:10,282
YES, IT IS!

196
00:08:10,324 --> 00:08:12,993
GENTLEMEN, PICK YOUR CATEGORY.

197
00:08:13,034 --> 00:08:15,412
"FEARS AND PET PEEVES."

198
00:08:15,454 --> 00:08:19,166
"WHAT IS MONICA'S
BIGGEST PET PEEVE?"

199
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:21,293
ANIMALS DRESSED AS HUMANS.

200
00:08:21,335 --> 00:08:23,253
Ross:
THAT'S CORRECT.

201
00:08:23,295 --> 00:08:25,255
LADIES?

202
00:08:25,297 --> 00:08:26,465
SAME CATEGORY.

203
00:08:28,258 --> 00:08:29,676
"ACCORDING TO CHANDLER

204
00:08:29,717 --> 00:08:32,887
WHAT PHENOMENON SCARES
THE BEJEEZUS OUT OF HIM?"

205
00:08:34,389 --> 00:08:37,600
MICHAEL FLATLEY,
LORD OF THE DANCE.

206
00:08:37,642 --> 00:08:39,478
THAT IS CORRECT.

207
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:41,229
AH!
WHOO!

208
00:08:41,271 --> 00:08:44,524
THE IRISH JIG GUY?

209
00:08:44,565 --> 00:08:46,026
HIS LEGS FLAIL ABOUT

210
00:08:46,067 --> 00:08:48,528
AS IF INDEPENDENT
FROM HIS BODY.

211
00:08:48,569 --> 00:08:50,280
AW!

212
00:08:50,322 --> 00:08:51,823
GENTLEMEN, YOUR PICK.

213
00:08:51,865 --> 00:08:53,450
"IT'S ALL RELATIVE."

214
00:08:53,492 --> 00:08:56,953
"MONICA AND I HAD
A GRANDMOTHER WHO DIED.

215
00:08:56,995 --> 00:08:59,247
"YOU BOTH WENT
TO HER FUNERAL.

216
00:08:59,289 --> 00:09:00,957
NAME THAT GRANDMOTHER."

217
00:09:03,710 --> 00:09:04,794
NANA?

218
00:09:04,836 --> 00:09:07,339
SHE HAS A REAL NAME.

219
00:09:07,381 --> 00:09:10,175
-ALTHEA!
-ALTHEA? WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

220
00:09:10,217 --> 00:09:10,675
I TOOK A SHOT.

221
00:09:10,717 --> 00:09:11,926
WITH ALTHEA?

222
00:09:11,968 --> 00:09:12,886
ALTHEA IS CORRECT.

223
00:09:12,927 --> 00:09:14,388
NICE SHOOTING!

224
00:09:18,099 --> 00:09:19,476
WE'LL TAKE
"LITERATURE!"

225
00:09:19,518 --> 00:09:21,520
"EVERY WEEK THE TV GUIDE

226
00:09:21,560 --> 00:09:24,772
"COMES TO CHANDLER
AND JOEY'S APARTMENT.

227
00:09:24,814 --> 00:09:28,109
WHAT NAME APPEARS
ON THE ADDRESS LABEL?"

228
00:09:28,151 --> 00:09:29,152
CHANDLER GETS IT!

229
00:09:29,194 --> 00:09:30,362
IT'S CHANDLER BING!

230
00:09:30,404 --> 00:09:31,988
NO!

231
00:09:32,030 --> 00:09:36,117
I'M AFRAID THE TV GUIDE
COMES TO "CHANANDLER BONG."

232
00:09:38,078 --> 00:09:39,704
I KNEW THAT.

233
00:09:39,746 --> 00:09:42,832
RACHEL, USE YOUR HEAD.

234
00:09:42,874 --> 00:09:47,003
ACTUALLY, IT'S
"MISS CHANANDLER BONG."

235
00:09:54,428 --> 00:09:56,679
HELLO, TEENY EMBRYOS.

236
00:09:58,181 --> 00:10:00,559
WELL, I'M PHOEBE BUFFAY. HI.

237
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:05,939
I'M-I'M HOPING TO BE YOUR UTERUS
FOR THE NEXT NINE MONTHS, SO...

238
00:10:05,980 --> 00:10:09,150
YOU SHOULD KNOW THAT WE'RE
DOING THIS FOR FRANK AND ALICE

239
00:10:09,192 --> 00:10:11,736
WHO YOU KNOW--
YOU'VE BEEN THERE.

240
00:10:13,238 --> 00:10:15,073
UM...

241
00:10:15,115 --> 00:10:17,534
YOU KNOW, THEY WANT YOU SO MUCH.

242
00:10:17,576 --> 00:10:21,079
SO WHEN YOU GUYS GET IN THERE,
REALLY GRAB ON.

243
00:10:21,121 --> 00:10:23,123
OKAY, AND... AND I PROMISE

244
00:10:23,164 --> 00:10:25,542
THAT I'LL KEEP YOU
SAFE AND WARM

245
00:10:25,584 --> 00:10:29,421
UNTIL, YOU KNOW, YOU'RE READY
TO HAVE THEM TAKE YOU HOME.

246
00:10:29,463 --> 00:10:31,089
SO...

247
00:10:31,131 --> 00:10:32,757
OKAY.

248
00:10:32,799 --> 00:10:35,218
OH, AND ALSO,
NEXT TIME YOU SEE ME

249
00:10:35,260 --> 00:10:37,512
IF I'M SCREAMING, DON'T WORRY.

250
00:10:37,554 --> 00:10:39,931
THAT'S WHAT'S SUPPOSED
TO HAPPEN.

251
00:10:39,973 --> 00:10:41,266
( knocking )

252
00:10:41,308 --> 00:10:42,267
READY?

253
00:10:42,309 --> 00:10:43,602
UH-HUH.

254
00:10:43,642 --> 00:10:45,228
GOOD LUCK.

255
00:10:46,605 --> 00:10:47,981
ALL RIGHT.

256
00:10:48,022 --> 00:10:50,775
THE SCORE IS NINE TO EIGHT
IN FAVOR OF THE GUYS.

257
00:10:50,817 --> 00:10:53,528
LADIES, IF YOU MISS THIS,
THE GAME IS THEIRS.

258
00:10:53,570 --> 00:10:54,695
PICK YOUR CATEGORY.

259
00:10:54,737 --> 00:10:55,822
"IT'S ALL RELATIVE!"

260
00:10:57,324 --> 00:10:59,618
YOU DON'T HAVE
TO SHOUT EVERYTHING.

261
00:10:59,659 --> 00:11:01,495
I'M SORRY!

262
00:11:03,497 --> 00:11:04,623
OOH.

263
00:11:04,664 --> 00:11:06,207
"WHAT IS THE NAME

264
00:11:06,249 --> 00:11:11,296
OF CHANDLER'S FATHER'S
LAS VEGAS ALL-MALE BURLESQUE?"

265
00:11:11,338 --> 00:11:14,673
VIVA LAS GAYGAS!

266
00:11:16,259 --> 00:11:18,719
UNFORTUNATELY,
THAT IS CORRECT.

267
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:20,388
YES!
YES!

268
00:11:20,430 --> 00:11:22,015
ALL RIGHT.

269
00:11:22,056 --> 00:11:23,642
WE HAVE A TIE.

270
00:11:23,682 --> 00:11:28,146
LUCKILY, I'VE PREPARED
FOR SUCH AN EVENT.

271
00:11:28,188 --> 00:11:30,565
THE LIGHTNING ROUND!

272
00:11:30,607 --> 00:11:31,732
OH!
OH!

273
00:11:33,734 --> 00:11:35,028
3O SECONDS.

274
00:11:35,069 --> 00:11:37,531
ALL THE QUESTIONS
YOU CAN ANSWER.

275
00:11:37,572 --> 00:11:39,616
YOU GUYS ARE DEAD.

276
00:11:39,658 --> 00:11:42,202
I AM SO GOOD
AT LIGHTNING ROUNDS.

277
00:11:43,702 --> 00:11:46,289
I MAJORED
IN LIGHTNING ROUNDS, ALL RIGHT?

278
00:11:46,331 --> 00:11:48,082
WE'RE GOING TO DESTROY YOU.

279
00:11:48,124 --> 00:11:49,292
WANT TO BET?

280
00:11:49,334 --> 00:11:50,460
I'M SO CONFUSED

281
00:11:50,502 --> 00:11:53,171
AS TO WHAT
WE'VE BEEN DOING SO FAR.

282
00:11:53,213 --> 00:11:55,840
HOW ABOUT WE PLAY
FOR MORE MONEY?

283
00:11:55,882 --> 00:11:58,009
SAY, 150?

284
00:11:58,051 --> 00:12:00,719
ONE HUNDRED AND
FIFTY DOLLARS.

285
00:12:02,222 --> 00:12:04,057
SAY, 200?

286
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:06,267
TWO HUNDRED DOLLARS.

287
00:12:06,309 --> 00:12:08,311
YOU'RE DOING IT AGAIN.

288
00:12:08,353 --> 00:12:10,104
EXCUSE ME.

289
00:12:10,146 --> 00:12:12,440
MONICA, I DON'T WANT
TO LOSE $200.

290
00:12:12,482 --> 00:12:13,525
WE WON'T.

291
00:12:13,567 --> 00:12:14,733
300?

292
00:12:14,775 --> 00:12:16,695
MONICA!

293
00:12:16,735 --> 00:12:18,321
I'M JUST TRYING
TO SPICE IT UP.

294
00:12:18,363 --> 00:12:19,364
OKAY, SO THEN PLAY
FOR SOME PEPPER.

295
00:12:19,406 --> 00:12:22,867
STOP SPENDING MY MONEY.

296
00:12:22,909 --> 00:12:24,035
I GOT IT.

297
00:12:24,077 --> 00:12:25,537
HOW ABOUT IF WE WIN

298
00:12:25,579 --> 00:12:28,206
THEY HAVE TO GET RID
OF THE ROOSTER?

299
00:12:28,248 --> 00:12:30,124
OOH, THAT'S INTERESTING.

300
00:12:30,166 --> 00:12:32,377
HEY, NO WAY.
THAT ROOSTER'S FAMILY.

301
00:12:32,419 --> 00:12:33,461
THROW IN THE DUCK.

302
00:12:33,503 --> 00:12:35,630
THE DUCK DOESN'T
MAKE ANY NOISE.

303
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:38,049
WELL, HE GETS
THE OTHER ONE ALL RILED UP.

304
00:12:38,091 --> 00:12:39,509
LOOK, WE ARE NOT...

305
00:12:39,551 --> 00:12:41,094
ALL RIGHT, HOLD ON.

306
00:12:43,096 --> 00:12:45,557
IF YOU WIN, WE'LL
GIVE UP THE BIRDS.

307
00:12:45,599 --> 00:12:47,016
GAH!

308
00:12:49,477 --> 00:12:51,396
BUT IF WE WIN...

309
00:12:51,438 --> 00:12:53,273
WE GET YOUR APARTMENT.

310
00:12:53,314 --> 00:12:54,649
OOH.

311
00:12:56,651 --> 00:12:57,818
DEAL!

312
00:13:02,699 --> 00:13:04,951
MONICA, BETTING
THE APARTMENT?

313
00:13:04,992 --> 00:13:07,454
I HAVE NOT MISSED ONE QUESTION
THE WHOLE GAME.

314
00:13:07,495 --> 00:13:09,706
I OWN THIS GAME!

315
00:13:09,748 --> 00:13:10,624
LOOK AT MY HAND.

316
00:13:10,665 --> 00:13:12,041
ARE THE ANSWERS

317
00:13:12,083 --> 00:13:14,377
WRITTEN ON THERE?

318
00:13:14,419 --> 00:13:16,129
NO! STEADY AS A ROCK.

319
00:13:16,170 --> 00:13:17,880
NOW, ARE YOU WITH ME?

320
00:13:17,922 --> 00:13:19,798
HUH! LET'S DO IT!

321
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:21,593
COME ON!
OKAY.

322
00:13:21,635 --> 00:13:24,053
ALL RIGHT, GENTLEMEN,
YOU'RE UP FIRST.

323
00:13:24,095 --> 00:13:25,305
OKAY.
OKAY.

324
00:13:25,346 --> 00:13:27,724
YOU HAVE 30 SECONDS.

325
00:13:27,766 --> 00:13:29,768
THE LIGHTNING ROUND

326
00:13:29,808 --> 00:13:31,645
BEGINS... STOP IT.

327
00:13:34,439 --> 00:13:35,898
NOW. WHAT
WAS MONICA'S NICKNAME

328
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,651
WHEN SHE WAS
A FIELD HOCKEY GOALIE?

329
00:13:37,692 --> 00:13:39,026
"BIG FAT GOALIE."
CORRECT.

330
00:13:41,904 --> 00:13:44,783
RACHEL CLAIMS
THIS IS HER FAVORITE MOVIE.

331
00:13:44,823 --> 00:13:46,409
DANGEROUS LIAISONS.

332
00:13:46,451 --> 00:13:47,910
HER ACTUAL FAVORITE MOVIE IS?

333
00:13:47,952 --> 00:13:49,245
WEEKEND AT BERNIE'S.

334
00:13:49,287 --> 00:13:51,080
CORRECT.

335
00:13:51,122 --> 00:13:52,791
IN WHAT PART OF HER BODY

336
00:13:52,831 --> 00:13:55,627
DID MONICA GET A PENCIL STUCK
AT AGE 14?

337
00:13:55,669 --> 00:13:56,753
OH!

338
00:13:59,547 --> 00:14:00,965
EW! NO!

339
00:14:03,134 --> 00:14:04,385
HER EAR!

340
00:14:06,304 --> 00:14:07,430
ALL RIGHT.

341
00:14:07,472 --> 00:14:09,599
MONICA CATEGORIZES HER TOWELS.

342
00:14:09,641 --> 00:14:11,768
HOW MANY CATEGORIES ARE THERE?

343
00:14:11,810 --> 00:14:12,769
"EVERYDAY USE."

344
00:14:12,811 --> 00:14:13,812
"GUEST."
"FANCY."

345
00:14:13,852 --> 00:14:14,895
"FANCY GUEST."

346
00:14:14,937 --> 00:14:15,854
TWO SECONDS.

347
00:14:15,896 --> 00:14:16,981
D'UH, 11?!

348
00:14:17,023 --> 00:14:17,982
( beeping )

349
00:14:18,024 --> 00:14:19,275
11. UNBELIEVABLE.

350
00:14:19,317 --> 00:14:20,360
11 IS CORRECT.

351
00:14:20,401 --> 00:14:21,402
YES!
( laughing )

352
00:14:23,154 --> 00:14:25,948
ALL RIGHT, THAT'S FOUR
FOR THE GUYS.

353
00:14:25,990 --> 00:14:27,867
LADIES, YOU'RE UP.

354
00:14:27,908 --> 00:14:29,118
ALL RIGHT,
COME ON!

355
00:14:33,498 --> 00:14:35,458
30 SECONDS ON THE CLOCK.

356
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:38,545
FIVE CORRECT QUESTIONS
WINS THE GAME.

357
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:40,755
THE LIGHTNING ROUND
BEGINS...

358
00:14:40,797 --> 00:14:42,382
NOW.
WHAT IS JOEY'S FAVORITE FOOD?

359
00:14:42,423 --> 00:14:44,008
SANDWICHES.
CORRECT.

360
00:14:44,050 --> 00:14:45,218
CHANDLER WAS HOW OLD

361
00:14:45,259 --> 00:14:46,761
WHEN HE FIRST TOUCHED
A GIRL'S BREAST?

362
00:14:46,803 --> 00:14:48,262
FOURTEEN?
NO, 19.

363
00:14:48,304 --> 00:14:50,014
THANKS, MAN.

364
00:14:50,056 --> 00:14:52,475
JOEY HAD
AN IMAGINARY CHILDHOOD FRIEND.

365
00:14:52,517 --> 00:14:53,476
HIS NAME WAS...?

366
00:14:53,518 --> 00:14:54,394
MAURICE.

367
00:14:54,435 --> 00:14:55,520
HIS PROFESSION WAS...?

368
00:14:55,562 --> 00:14:56,855
SPACE COWBOY!
CORRECT!

369
00:14:58,815 --> 00:15:00,525
WHAT IS CHANDLER BING'S JOB?

370
00:15:03,152 --> 00:15:04,237
OH...!

371
00:15:04,278 --> 00:15:06,155
OH, GOSH! DOES
IT HAVE SOMETHING

372
00:15:06,197 --> 00:15:07,448
TO DO WITH NUMBERS?

373
00:15:07,490 --> 00:15:08,491
AND PROCESSING.

374
00:15:08,533 --> 00:15:09,868
AND HE CARRIES
A BRIEFCASE.

375
00:15:09,909 --> 00:15:11,786
YOU NEED THIS,
OR YOU LOSE THE GAME.

376
00:15:11,828 --> 00:15:14,831
IT HAS SOMETHING
TO DO WITH TRANSPONDING.

377
00:15:14,873 --> 00:15:17,834
OH, OH, HE'S
A TRANSPONDS-
TRANSPONSTER!

378
00:15:19,335 --> 00:15:21,546
THAT'S NOT EVEN A WORD!

379
00:15:21,588 --> 00:15:23,339
OH!

380
00:15:23,381 --> 00:15:25,717
I CAN GET THIS!
I CAN...

381
00:15:25,759 --> 00:15:26,801
( beeping )

382
00:15:26,843 --> 00:15:28,803
NO!!!

383
00:15:28,845 --> 00:15:30,179
YES!
YES!

384
00:15:42,483 --> 00:15:44,110
I CALL MONICA'S ROOM.

385
00:15:44,151 --> 00:15:46,028
YOU CAN'T JUST CALL
MONICA'S ROOM.

386
00:15:46,070 --> 00:15:47,113
SURE, I CAN.

387
00:15:47,154 --> 00:15:48,489
STANDARD SHOTGUN RULES.

388
00:15:48,531 --> 00:15:49,949
I'M IN SIGHT OF THE ROOM

389
00:15:49,990 --> 00:15:52,201
AND I CALLED IT.

390
00:15:54,537 --> 00:15:56,955
MAN, I FEEL LIKE I'M
COMING DOWN WITH SOMETHING.

391
00:15:56,997 --> 00:15:58,165
OOH.
YEAH.

392
00:15:58,207 --> 00:15:59,250
BET YOU CAN'T GUESS

393
00:15:59,292 --> 00:16:00,710
WHAT COLOR MY
TONSILS ARE.

394
00:16:00,752 --> 00:16:02,128
I'LL BET THE APARTMENT.

395
00:16:02,169 --> 00:16:03,797
I WOULD NEVER BET
THIS APARTMENT.

396
00:16:03,838 --> 00:16:04,923
IT'S TOO NICE.

397
00:16:07,133 --> 00:16:08,134
HEY.

398
00:16:08,175 --> 00:16:09,719
OOH, PHEEBS, ARE
THEY IN THERE?

399
00:16:09,761 --> 00:16:11,679
UM, YEAH, UH-HUH, I'M IMPLANTED.

400
00:16:11,721 --> 00:16:13,222
HOW DO YOU FEEL?

401
00:16:13,264 --> 00:16:15,308
WELL, FREAKED.

402
00:16:16,517 --> 00:16:19,228
IT TURNS OUT THE ODDS
ARE, LIKE, REALLY SUCKY

403
00:16:19,270 --> 00:16:22,106
AND THIS IS FRANK AND ALICE'S,
LIKE, ONLY SHOT.

404
00:16:22,148 --> 00:16:23,691
THEY ARE, LIKE, LITERALLY

405
00:16:23,733 --> 00:16:25,902
PUTTING ALL THEIR EGGS
IN MY BASKET.

406
00:16:25,944 --> 00:16:29,196
YEAH, BUT I BET
IT WORKS.

407
00:16:29,238 --> 00:16:30,949
REALLY? HOW MUCH?

408
00:16:32,074 --> 00:16:33,910
ALL RIGHT, I'M GOING TO GO

409
00:16:33,952 --> 00:16:36,203
TAKE A PREGNANCY TEST RIGHT NOW.

410
00:16:36,245 --> 00:16:38,289
OH, WOW. YOU CAN TELL THIS SOON?

411
00:16:38,331 --> 00:16:40,541
WELL, THE DOCTOR SAYS
IT TAKES A COUPLE DAYS

412
00:16:40,583 --> 00:16:42,627
BUT MY BODY'S
ALWAYS BEEN A LITTLE FASTER

413
00:16:42,669 --> 00:16:44,128
THAN WESTERN MEDICINE, SO...

414
00:16:46,798 --> 00:16:47,924
( clearing throat )

415
00:16:47,966 --> 00:16:48,967
OH, MY GOD.

416
00:16:49,007 --> 00:16:50,301
I CAN'T BELIEVE YOU GUYS

417
00:16:50,343 --> 00:16:52,386
ACTUALLY THINK
YOU'RE MOVING IN HERE.

418
00:16:52,428 --> 00:16:54,180
WELL, BELIEVE IT, BABY.

419
00:16:55,181 --> 00:16:57,809
WELL, I-I, I'M NOT MOVING.

420
00:16:57,851 --> 00:16:59,769
WHAT?!

421
00:16:59,811 --> 00:17:01,437
NO. IT WAS A STUPID BET.

422
00:17:01,479 --> 00:17:03,439
WE WERE JUST PLAYING A GAME.

423
00:17:03,481 --> 00:17:05,065
YOU CAN'T
JUST IGNORE THE BET.

424
00:17:05,107 --> 00:17:06,275
IT'S A BET.

425
00:17:06,317 --> 00:17:08,110
YOU BET ON A BET,
AND IF YOU LOSE

426
00:17:08,152 --> 00:17:09,904
YOU LOSE THE BET.

427
00:17:09,946 --> 00:17:11,322
RACH, WE HAVE TO MOVE.

428
00:17:11,364 --> 00:17:13,867
IF WE HAD LOST, WE
WOULD HAVE MADE THEM

429
00:17:13,908 --> 00:17:15,409
GET RID OF THE BIRDS,
RIGHT?

430
00:17:15,451 --> 00:17:16,661
NO.

431
00:17:18,621 --> 00:17:20,122
ALL RIGHT, LOOK, I HATE THIS

432
00:17:20,164 --> 00:17:23,125
AS MUCH AS YOU, BUT...
IF IT MAKES YOU FEEL ANY BETTER

433
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:24,460
THIS IS ALL YOUR FAULT.

434
00:17:26,379 --> 00:17:27,463
WHAT?!

435
00:17:27,505 --> 00:17:29,089
"CHANANDLER BONG."

436
00:17:29,131 --> 00:17:31,384
COME ON, WE STEAL
THAT TV GUIDE EVERY WEEK.

437
00:17:31,425 --> 00:17:33,052
I KNEW IT!

438
00:17:34,261 --> 00:17:35,471
I DON'T CARE.

439
00:17:35,513 --> 00:17:36,848
I'M NOT GOING ANYWHERE.

440
00:17:36,890 --> 00:17:39,559
COOL. GIRL ROOMMATE.

441
00:17:42,061 --> 00:17:43,145
WELL?

442
00:17:43,187 --> 00:17:45,314
NOPE, NOT
KNOCKED UP YET.

443
00:17:45,356 --> 00:17:47,901
ALL RIGHT, WELL,
IT'S ONLY BEEN A COUPLE HOURS

444
00:17:47,942 --> 00:17:49,443
SO, JUST GIVE IT SOME TIME.

445
00:17:49,485 --> 00:17:50,862
YEAH, ALL RIGHT.
MEANWHILE

446
00:17:50,904 --> 00:17:52,488
I'M GOING TO DO
WHATEVER I CAN

447
00:17:52,530 --> 00:17:54,991
TO HELP THIS, SO, I'M
JUST GOING TO, YOU KNOW

448
00:17:55,033 --> 00:17:56,283
LIE IN YOUR
CHAIR, OKAY?

449
00:17:57,410 --> 00:17:59,078
YOU KNOW, JUST...
YEAH, GOOD.

450
00:17:59,119 --> 00:18:01,998
I'M GOING TO LET GRAVITY,
YOU KNOW, DO ITS JOB.

451
00:18:06,627 --> 00:18:09,463
HEY, RACH, CAN YOU GIVE
ME A HAND WITH THIS BOX?

452
00:18:09,505 --> 00:18:11,131
NO! PUT THAT BOX DOWN!

453
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:13,175
WE ARE NOT GOING ANYWHERE!

454
00:18:14,886 --> 00:18:17,638
THIS IS MY APARTMENT,
AND I LIKE IT!

455
00:18:17,680 --> 00:18:19,974
THIS IS A "GIRLS'" APARTMENT!

456
00:18:20,016 --> 00:18:22,184
THAT IS A "BOYS'" APARTMENT!

457
00:18:22,226 --> 00:18:24,186
IT'S DIRTY AND IT SMELLS!

458
00:18:24,228 --> 00:18:25,438
THIS IS PRETTY!

459
00:18:25,479 --> 00:18:27,189
IT'S SO PRETTY!

460
00:18:27,231 --> 00:18:29,734
AND LOOK,
AND IT'S PURPLE!

461
00:18:29,776 --> 00:18:32,862
AND I'M TELLING YOU--
YOU WITH YOUR STEADY HAND--

462
00:18:32,904 --> 00:18:36,240
I AM NOT MOVING, AND NOW
I HAVE GOT THE STEADY HAND.

463
00:18:37,366 --> 00:18:38,492
I'LL TAKE CARE OF IT.

464
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:39,535
THAT'S RIGHT!

465
00:18:39,577 --> 00:18:41,579
YOU DO WHAT THE HAND SAYS!

466
00:18:43,247 --> 00:18:44,749
( door shuts )

467
00:18:52,715 --> 00:18:54,383
HOW'D IT GO?

468
00:18:54,425 --> 00:18:56,010
I LOST OUR MATTRESSES.

469
00:18:59,097 --> 00:19:01,307
( guitar strumming )

470
00:19:01,348 --> 00:19:03,267
♪ ARE YOU IN THERE,
LITTLE FETUS? ♪

471
00:19:03,309 --> 00:19:05,979
♪ IN NINE MONTHS,
WILL YOU COME GREET US...? ♪

472
00:19:07,772 --> 00:19:10,691
♪ I WILL BUY YOU
SOME ADIDAS... ♪

473
00:19:10,733 --> 00:19:12,318
( knock at door )

474
00:19:14,278 --> 00:19:15,571
HI.
HEY.

475
00:19:15,613 --> 00:19:18,032
OH, HI. PHOEBE, UM...

476
00:19:18,074 --> 00:19:20,034
WE WERE JUST
AT THE DRUGSTORE

477
00:19:20,076 --> 00:19:22,495
UM, SO WE GOT YOU
A LITTLE PRESENT.

478
00:19:22,536 --> 00:19:26,916
UM, IT'S A LOLLIPOP
AND, UH, A HOME PREGNANCY TEST.

479
00:19:26,958 --> 00:19:28,208
DON'T MIX THOSE UP.

480
00:19:28,250 --> 00:19:31,378
YOU COULD REALLY RUIN
THAT LOLLIPOP.

481
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:37,426
SO, UM... YOU FEEL
LIKE TAKING A TEST?

482
00:19:37,468 --> 00:19:39,679
THERE'S ONLY ONE QUESTION.

483
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:41,430
( goofy laughter )

484
00:19:41,472 --> 00:19:42,682
A-ALL RIGHT, I WILL.

485
00:19:42,723 --> 00:19:44,851
I WILL, BUT, UM,
YOU KNOW, JUST REMEMBER

486
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:46,519
THAT IT'S STILL REALLY EARLY

487
00:19:46,560 --> 00:19:48,562
SO, IF IT SAYS THAT
I'M NOT PREGNANT

488
00:19:48,604 --> 00:19:51,273
THAT DOESN'T MEAN I'M
NOT GOING TO GET PREGNANT

489
00:19:51,315 --> 00:19:53,442
OKAY? AND, AND
JUST PLEASE

490
00:19:53,484 --> 00:19:55,611
JUST SO I DON'T GO
COMPLETELY NUTS

491
00:19:55,653 --> 00:19:58,322
JUST TRY NOT TO PUT
ALL YOUR HOPES ON THIS

492
00:19:58,364 --> 00:19:59,406
OKAY?

493
00:19:59,448 --> 00:20:01,784
OKAY.
OKAY.

494
00:20:01,826 --> 00:20:03,661
GREAT.

495
00:20:10,208 --> 00:20:11,544
( laughing )

496
00:20:11,585 --> 00:20:12,837
YOU KNOW WHAT?

497
00:20:12,879 --> 00:20:16,007
YOU ARE MEAN BOYS
WHO ARE JUST BEING MEAN.

498
00:20:16,049 --> 00:20:17,383
HEY, DON'T
GET MAD AT US.

499
00:20:17,424 --> 00:20:19,510
NO ONE FORCED YOU
TO RAISE THE STAKES.

500
00:20:19,552 --> 00:20:20,845
THAT IS NOT TRUE!

501
00:20:20,887 --> 00:20:22,429
SHE DID! SHE FORCED ME!

502
00:20:22,471 --> 00:20:25,016
WE'D STILL BE HERE,
BUT YOU GOT THE QUESTION WRONG.

503
00:20:25,058 --> 00:20:27,518
WELL, IT WAS
A STUPID, UNFAIR QUESTION.

504
00:20:27,560 --> 00:20:29,353
DON'T BLAME
THE QUESTIONS.

505
00:20:29,395 --> 00:20:31,939
WOULD YOU ALL STOP YELLING
IN OUR APARTMENT?!

506
00:20:31,981 --> 00:20:33,900
YOU ARE RUINING
MOVING DAY FOR US!

507
00:20:33,941 --> 00:20:35,693
STOP CALLING IT YOUR APARTMENT!

508
00:20:35,735 --> 00:20:36,694
IT IS OUR APARTMENT!

509
00:20:36,736 --> 00:20:38,738
( everybody yelling )

510
00:20:38,779 --> 00:20:41,490
YOU GUYS, YOU GUYS,
YOU'RE GOING TO HAVE A BABY.

511
00:20:41,532 --> 00:20:43,159
THEY'RE GOING
TO HAVE A BABY!

512
00:20:49,415 --> 00:20:52,292
MY SISTER'S
GOING TO HAVE MY BABY!

513
00:21:00,760 --> 00:21:03,804
OKAY, BUT THIS
CAN'T BE GOOD FOR THE BABY.

514
00:21:05,765 --> 00:21:07,558
( cheering )

515
00:21:16,609 --> 00:21:18,569
I CAN'T FIND GARBAGE BAGS.

516
00:21:18,611 --> 00:21:20,780
OH, WELL, I THINK
I SAW SOME IN HERE.

517
00:21:20,821 --> 00:21:22,073
( screaming )

518
00:21:25,451 --> 00:21:27,369
WHAT IS IT?

519
00:21:27,411 --> 00:21:28,788
I DON'T KNOW

520
00:21:28,829 --> 00:21:30,248
BUT MAYBE IF
WE KEEP THAT
DRAWER SHUT

521
00:21:30,289 --> 00:21:31,791
IT'LL DIE.

522
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:36,294
I CAN'T BELIEVE
WE'RE LIVING HERE!

523
00:21:39,840 --> 00:21:41,259
( yelling )

524
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:43,219
WHA...? WH-WHAT IS IT?!

525
00:21:43,261 --> 00:21:45,138
DID YOU SEE THE SIZE
OF THE CLOSETS?!

526
00:21:46,931 --> 00:21:49,725
I CAN'T BELIEVE
WE LIVE HERE!

527
00:21:49,767 --> 00:21:53,771
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

528
00:21:55,397 --> 00:21:57,608
OH...!
OH...!

529
00:21:57,650 --> 00:21:59,652
OH!!!
OH!!!

